---
Basic

- mov dst, src         # Copy from src to dst (Move)
- lea dst, [src]       # Calculate address from memory but not read from it.
Exmp: lea rax, [rdi + rsi * 4 + 8]
- add dst, src         # Add: dst = dst + src
- sub dst, src         # Subtract: dst = dst - src
- imul dst, src        # Signed multiply
- inc reg / dec reg    # Increment / Decrement: +1 / -1
- ret                  # Return from func.


---
Compare instruction (adds RFLAGS)

- cmp a, b             # Compare: a - b. Result not returning, add flags ( = 0; > 0; overflow etc)
- test a, b            # Test; do bite AND: a & b. test rax, rax - check if rax eq 0 or negative


---
Conditions j*

For signed (i32, i64)             | For unsigned (u32, u64)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
jg  = Jump if Greater >           | ja  = Jump if Above >
jge = Jump if Greater or Equal >= | jae = Jump if Above or Equal >=
jl  = Jump if Less <              | jb  = Jump if Below <
jle = Jump if Less or Equal <=    | jbe = Jump if Below or Equal <=

jmp       = Unconditional Jump (always jump)
je / jz   = Jump if Equal / Jump if Zero 
jne / jnz = Jump if Not Equal / Jump if Not Zero
js / jns  = Jump if Sign / Not Sign


---
Intel Syntax

[ base + index * scale + displacement ]

Example: [ rbx + rcx * 8 + 16 ]
take address from rbx, add rcx * 8 and add 16. Then read/write on this address

QWORD PTR [rax] indicates size
- BYTE PTR  = 1 byte
- WORD PTR  = 2 bytes
- DWORD PTR = 4 bytes
- QWORD PTR = 8 bytes
